   {
    "card": {
     "title": "Does the news cover what kills us?"
    }
   },
   {
    "draw": [
     "axes"
    ],
    "voice": "a",
    "speak": "Does the news cover what actually kills us? Take every story the New York Times ran in 2023 that mentions a cause of death."
   },
   {
    "draw": [
     "tag_news"
    ],
    "voice": "b",
    "speak": "Surely it does. Journalists cover what matters."
   },
   {
    "ask": {
     "question": "You are the editor: share out a hundred stories between these causes.",
     "on": "all",
     "budget": 100,
     "judge": false,
     "account_label": "Stories left",
     "store": "ed",
     "right": "Here is how the Times really split them: homicide alone got forty-two of every hundred."
    }
   },
   {
    "highlight": {
     "target": [
      "bar_4",
      "bar_1",
      "bar_2"
     ]
    },
    "voice": "b",
    "speak": "Eighteen for terrorism? And heart disease and cancer get seven between them?"
   },
   {
    "erase": [
     "tag_news"
    ]
   },
   {
    "draw": [
     "ghosts",
     "gh_l",
     "tag_deaths"
    ],
    "voice": "a",
    "speak": "Keep the news as dashes. Now the bars show what Americans actually died of that year."
   },
   {
    "animate": {
     "stage": 1
    },
    "duration": 3,
    "voice": "a",
    "speak": "Heart disease and cancer shoot up: more than half of all these deaths."
   },
   {
    "highlight": {
     "target": [
      "bar_3"
     ]
    },
    "voice": "b",
    "speak": "And homicide, the paper's biggest bar, sinks to about one in a hundred."
   },
   {
    "draw": [
     "t16",
     "t18k"
    ],
    "voice": "a",
    "speak": "Terrorism killed sixteen people in the whole country. Its share of the news was about eighteen thousand times its share of the deaths."
   },
   {
    "erase": [
     "t16",
     "t18k"
    ]
   },
   {
    "voice": "b",
    "speak": "Fine, the Times is odd. Surely the other papers are different?",
    "highlight": {
     "target": [
      "tag_deaths"
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "draw": [
     "papers"
    ],
    "voice": "a",
    "speak": "The Washington Post and Fox News look much the same."
   },
   {
    "erase": [
     "papers"
    ]
   },
